  {
    "model": "challenge.challenge",
    "pk": 1,
    "fields": {
      "published_project": 21,
      "slug": "demo-ecg-challenge",
      "organizer": [
        "george"
      ],
      "organizer_name": "Co-hosted by PhysioNet and the National Institutes of Health",
      "registration_open_datetime": "2024-01-15T10:00:00Z",
      "start_datetime": "2024-02-01T00:00:00Z",
      "official_start_datetime": "2024-06-01T00:00:00Z",
      "end_datetime": "2025-09-01T23:59:59Z",
      "phase": "unofficial",
      "training_dataset": null,
      "validation_data_gcs_uri": "challenge-staging/challenges/ahe-prediction-challenge/validation/",
      "test_data_gcs_uri": "challenge-staging/challenges/ahe-prediction-challenge/test/",
      "validation_labels_gcs_uri": "challenge-staging/challenges/ahe-prediction-challenge/validation_labels/",
      "test_labels_gcs_uri": "challenge-staging/challenges/ahe-prediction-challenge/test_labels/",
      "rules": "<h3>Eligibility</h3><p>The challenge is open to all individuals and teams worldwide. Organizers and their immediate collaborators are not eligible for prizes but may submit entries for benchmarking purposes.</p><h3>Submissions</h3><ul><li>Each participant or team may submit up to <strong>5 entries per day</strong> and <strong>100 entries total</strong> during the unofficial phase.</li><li>Submissions must be fully automated\u2014no manual annotation or interactive steps are permitted.</li><li>Code must be original work by the submitting participant or team. Use of pre-trained models is permitted provided the training data and model weights are publicly available and cited.</li></ul><h3>Evaluation</h3><ul><li>During the unofficial phase, submissions are scored against the <em>validation</em> dataset. Scores on the validation set are shown on the public leaderboard.</li><li>During the official phase, selected submissions are re-evaluated against the <em>hidden test</em> dataset. Final rankings are based on test-set performance.</li><li>Organizers advance the top validation-scoring submissions for official-phase evaluation.</li></ul><h3>Publication</h3><p>All participants with accepted entries are invited to submit a short paper describing their methods to the Computing in Cardiology conference. Top-performing methods will be highlighted in a summary paper authored by the organizers.</p>",
      "evaluation_description": "<h3>Metrics</h3><p>The primary evaluation metric is the <strong>area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (AUROC)</strong>, which measures discrimination between AHE-positive and AHE-negative records across all operating thresholds.</p><p>Secondary metrics reported for each submission:</p><ul><li><strong>Sensitivity</strong> (recall): proportion of true AHE events correctly identified, at a decision threshold of 0.5.</li><li><strong>Positive Predictive Value</strong> (precision): proportion of predicted AHE events that were true events, at a decision threshold of 0.5.</li></ul><h3>Scoring Procedure</h3><p>Each submission container receives the test records as input and must write a <code>predictions.json</code> file containing one object per record with <code>record_id</code>, <code>prediction</code> (0 or 1), and <code>risk_score</code> (float between 0 and 1). The evaluation script computes AUROC from the <code>risk_score</code> column and derives sensitivity and PPV from the <code>prediction</code> column.</p>",
      "prizes": "<p><strong>First place:</strong> $5,000 and an invitation to present at Computing in Cardiology.</p><p><strong>Second place:</strong> $2,500.</p><p><strong>Third place:</strong> $1,000.</p><p>All prizes are sponsored by the National Institute of Biomedical Imaging and Bioengineering (NIBIB).</p>",
      "max_submissions_per_day": 5,
      "max_total_submissions": 100,
      "teams_enabled": true,
      "is_active": true,
      "created_datetime": "2024-01-15T10:00:00Z",
      "modified_datetime": "2024-03-10T14:30:00Z"
    }
  },
